  "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the optical lattice clock and its realization as an exceptional instrument for precision measurement"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B018",
    "B011"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B014 remains my preferred achievement. The magic-wavelength lattice clock is an elegant solution to a fundamental problem of atomic control: retaining many atoms for high signal while suppressing the trapping-induced frequency shift. Katori's conceptual contribution and Ye's defining experimental development give a compact attribution. The result is no longer a promising metrological device but a reproducible precision platform, developed independently in several laboratories, with credible reach to tests of fundamental physics as well as timekeeping and relativistic geodesy.",
    "case_against": "The strongest reservation is attribution: optical-frequency metrology rests on a wider lineage of clock pioneers and infrastructure than two names can represent. Its most visible institutional outcome, a redefinition of the second, is also still a future standards decision rather than a completed consequence.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson ranks B007 first, emphasizing circuit QED as a mature, controllable regime of artificial-atom and microwave-photon interaction, while noting that the appropriate boundary of credit includes Steven M. Girvin and others.",
        "response": "I agree that circuit QED is a profound and experimentally mature quantum-optics achievement. The unresolved attribution is nevertheless material: its decisive theory, experimental architecture, and related superconducting-circuit advances are difficult to delimit within three people. B014 has a sharper physical invention and a more bounded pairing, while retaining comparable experimental maturity."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson places B035 first because inflation and the quantum origin of cosmic structure have shaped precision cosmology, while recognizing that no unique microscopic inflationary mechanism has been identified experimentally.",
        "response": "The cosmological influence is indisputable, but that uncertainty goes to the heart of what is experimentally established. I would hesitate to honor a broad framework before its physical realization is identified. Optical lattice clocks instead offer a precise, repeatedly verified physical advance whose limits and systematic effects can be directly tested."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that B011 enabled ultrafast science through titanium-sapphire lasers and passive femtosecond mode locking, but notes the broader development lineage.",
        "response": "I value B011 highly because ultrafast sources made new temporal physics accessible. Yet the proposed achievement joins a laser medium with several distinct mode-locking advances, making a single citation and three-person allocation less clean than the lattice-clock case."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether a historical review would confirm that Katori and Ye alone best delimit the central optical-lattice-clock achievement amid wider optical-clock contributions."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "I have collaborated with Ursula Keller's group, a connection relevant to alternative B011; I therefore do not advocate B011 as my preferred configuration."
  }
}
